<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Toronto Open POI &mdash; candidate explorer</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="explorer.css">
<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
      integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY="
      crossorigin="">
<script defer src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
        integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo="
        crossorigin=""></script>
<script defer src="explorer.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="app">

<header class="bar">
  <div class="bar-head">
    <h1>Toronto Open POI &mdash; what DineSafe and BodySafe would add to OSM</h1>
    <span class="built">built {{BUILD_DATE}}</span>
  </div>
  <div class="counts">
    <div class="count new"><strong id="n-new">{{NEW}}</strong><span>would create</span></div>
    <div class="count enrich"><strong id="n-enrich">{{ENRICH}}</strong><span>would address</span></div>
    <div class="count conflict"><strong id="n-conflict">{{CONFLICT}}</strong><span>name conflict</span></div>
    <div class="count matched"><strong id="n-matched">{{MATCHED}}</strong><span>already in OSM</span></div>
    <div class="count orphan"><strong id="n-orphan">{{ORPHAN}}</strong><span>OSM, unlicensed</span></div>
    <div class="count notpoi"><strong id="n-not-poi">{{NOTPOI}}</strong><span>not a POI</span></div>
    <div class="count meta-count">
      Counts follow the filters. Of all {{NEW}} unmatched premises, <strong>{{CREATABLE}}</strong>
      are the defensible ones: category known, and not one of several premises sharing a mall
      or stadium address. The filters start on that view.
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<p class="warn">
  <strong>A survey queue, not an import.</strong> Nothing here has been checked against
  the ground: the matching is automated, the categories are inferred from what a premise
  is <em>licensed</em> as rather than what its shopfront says, the names are reconstructed
  from capitals, and about a third of the positions are a health-unit geocode rather than
  a surveyed point. If you are editing OpenStreetMap from this, read the
  <a href="https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Import/Guidelines">Import Guidelines</a> and
  the <a href="https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Automated_Edits_code_of_conduct">Automated
  Edits code of conduct</a> first. No import has been proposed, and this is not one.
</p>

<div class="layout">
  <div id="map" data-geojson="candidates.geojson"></div>

  <aside class="panel">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <div class="controls">
        <label><span class="swatch new"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-new" checked> Would create</label>
        <label><span class="swatch enrich"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-enrich" checked> Would address</label>
        <label><span class="swatch conflict"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-conflict" checked> Name conflict</label>
        <label><span class="swatch matched"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-matched"> Already in OSM</label>
        <label><span class="swatch orphan"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-orphan"> OSM, unlicensed</label>
        <label><span class="swatch notpoi"></span>
          <input type="checkbox" id="show-not-poi"> Not a POI</label>
      </div>
      <div class="controls controls-2">
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="hide-venues" checked> Hide venue stalls (5+ per address)</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="show-unknown"> Include unknown category</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="only-food"> DineSafe only</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" id="only-body"> BodySafe only</label>
        <input type="search" id="filter" placeholder="Filter by name, address or type...">
      </div>
      <p class="hint">
        The table lists what is on screen; <span class="pill add">+n</span> is tags the
        licence would add, <span class="pill diff">&ne;n</span> tags the two disagree on.
        Click a row to centre it and open the full tag comparison, then
        <kbd>O</kbd> opens that spot on openstreetmap.org and <kbd>I</kbd> in the iD
        editor &mdash; on the matched element where there is one, at the address
        point where there is not. Hollow dots were not found in the City address
        gazetteer, so their position is the health unit's own geocode and may be off
        by tens of metres; small pale dots are premises whose category DineSafe
        dropped in 2023 and the archive cannot recover. <strong>Nothing here is verified against the ground;
        it is a survey queue, not an import.</strong>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table id="rows">
        <thead>
          <tr><th class="col-name">Name</th><th>Address</th>
              <th>Tags</th><th>OSM &middot; iD</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="tally"></p>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>

<footer class="credits">
  Contains information made available under the
  <a href="https://open.toronto.ca/open-data-license/">Open Government Licence &ndash; Toronto</a>
